    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Author Mark Twain lived in Unionville for a brief time in 1862 while prospecting for silver without much success.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unionville%2C_Nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Unionville served as the original county seat for Humboldt County from its founding in 1861 until 1873.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unionville%2C_Nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A big mining boom occurred in Unionville between 1863 and 1870, making it an active prospecting center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unionville%2C_Nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The completion of the Central Pacific Railroad through the Humboldt valley speeded the decline of Unionville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
